I see that the object specs are created with `createSetOptionsSpec`, which doesn't set `effects`. The `effects` field in `ObjectRegistrationSpec` is optional. Looking at the flow:

In `ObjectSetup.ts` line 200:
```typescript
if (resolvedConfig.effects && typeof object.setEffects === "function") {
  object.setEffects(resolvedConfig.effects);
}
```

This requires `resolvedConfig.effects` to be set. The `resolvedConfig` comes from `ObjectConfigRuntime`. Let me check if any objects have bloom configured there.


Based on what I've seen, no objects explicitly have bloom enabled via `setEffects()`, so `bloomRoots` should always be empty and selective bloom never runs. The base class `getBloomEnabled()` returns `this._effects.bloom?.enabled ?? false`, which would be false if no effects are set. Even if JetEngine has internal bloom meshes, its `getBloomEnabled()` still uses the base class logic requiring `this._effects.bloom?.enabled === true`, so that's separate from this check.

Let me trace through what `ObjectConfigRuntime` actually returns for effects to see if `hasRoots` could ever be true.

