```typescript
if (!hasRoots) {
  this._renderer.render(this._scene, this._camera);
  return;
}
```

Wait, this is weird. The PostProcessor uses `selective` bloom but no objects have bloom enabled. So the bloom pass is never called. The vignette is also not applied (it's in the `_finalComposer`).


Actually, let me trace through the render method more carefully. The method checks if `_bloomPass` exists first, and if not, it either uses the composer or falls back to direct rendering. Then if selective bloom is enabled, it checks for renderable bloom roots and calls the selective render path.

The key issue is that the vignette effect only runs in `_finalComposer`, which is only invoked when `hasRoots=true`. So if the hero scene objects don't have bloom enabled in their config, the vignette won't appear at all. I should check what effects are actually configured for those objects in the page config.

