Key finding! Looking at `Scene.addObject()`:
```typescript
async addObject(id: string, object: SceneObject): Promise<void> {
  this._objects.set(id, object);  // line 27 - stores SceneObject
  // ...
  const obj = ...; // line 36 - also stores animation target in rawObjects
  this._rawObjects.set(id, obj);
```

Wait, it stores in BOTH! It stores `object` in `_objects` AND something in `_rawObjects`. Then `scene.getObject()` checks `_rawObjects` FIRST, then `_objects.getAnimationTarget()`.


So if CloudPlane is stored in `_rawObjects` with its animation target (THREE.Group), then `scene.getObject(cloudId)` returns the THREE.Group, and `_applyScalarProps(group, { chapter: 0, transition: 0 })` sets those properties directly on the THREE.Group. Now I need to check whether CloudPlane actually reads from its timeline root group to understand how these properties flow through.

